# "Counter target artifact or enchantment spell": only a spell, and only one of those types. On turn three Bot1 casts
# Llanowar Elves with Bot2's Island open and a Sol Ring on the battlefield: neither the creature spell nor the Sol Ring
# permanent (not a spell) is a target, so Annul is not offered at all. Then Rancor, an enchantment spell, is cast on the
# Elves and the same Annul, with the same mana, counters it (the positive control). It ends in Bot1's graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Forest
Sol Ring
Llanowar Elves
Rancor
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Annul
Island x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
! Bot2.Hand.Annul.Cast(Stack.Llanowar Elves)
! Bot2.Hand.Annul.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring)
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Rancor.Cast(Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Annul.Cast(Stack.Rancor)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Rancor
Bot2.Graveyard = Annul
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Forest; Sol Ring; Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Power = 1
